// pfodWeb NOTE: this board only exists in the real Arduino IDE as a
// "Revision" submenu option under a different parent board id (no
// standalone <id>.name= boards.txt entry of its own), so the normal
// boards.txt id lookup can't give it a unique name — without this
// override it would silently collide with every other board sharing
// this chip's default boardName.
// Also removed from the chip-level default chipGpios map: the
// onboard microSD card's SPI bus (2,11,13,14) and the LR1121 (SCK/MISO/MOSI/CS/RST/DIO9/BUSY)
// radio module's own SPI+control lines.
// Full copy of variants/esp32/esp32s3/board.json with boardName/
// displayName changed and the above chipGpios entries removed.
// pfodWeb NOTE: GPIO0 tagged "button" - confirmed onboard BOOT button
// (customizable/user button) per LilyGo-LoRa-Series official hardware
// doc docs/en/t3_s3_lr1121/t3_s3_lr1121_hw.md. The board's other
// documented onboard LED (GPIO37) was NOT tagged: GPIO37 has no
// chipGpios entry because it falls within the chip-level default
// board.json's pre-existing pin-exclusion range (GPIO22-37); re-adding
// it would reverse that exclusion, which is out of scope here - see
// boardsDetails/esp32/esp32s3/lilygo_t3_s3_lr1121/notes.txt.
{
  "boardName": "LilyGoT3S3LR1121",
  "displayName": "LilyGo T3-S3 (LR1121)",
